Many Indians used to get electronic goods fixed, but now many products cannot be mended. A built-in obsolescence has broken the country's&#160;electronics repair infrastructure.

In a week from now, leaders and representatives of BRICS nations will descend upon New Delhi to attend the 18th summit of the international group which India is hosting as part of its 2026 presidency.

The summit will be held from September 12 to 13 at the Bharat Mandapam convention center in the Indian capital.&#160;

Preparations are entering their final stage ahead of the meet and Delhi is set to be a fortress with a heavy security blanket.

On Saturday, a motorcade rehearsal had been scheduled with the traffic authorities in Delhi issuing an advisory for diversions and regulated movement on key routes.&#160;

The Indian Express&#160; has reported that drones would be deployed to track the movement of traffic and spot chokepoints during the summit.&#160;

Meanwhile, media reports earlier this week said that hotel prices in the capital were soaring around the dates of the summit.

Indian news outlets said that luxury hotels in the city were either fully sold out or were giving rooms at a significantly higher tariff.&#160;

For one luxury hotel in central Delhi, a room that costs 23,000 Indian Rupees (€210, $243 approx) a night this weekend was listed at 280,000 Indian Rupees (€2,550, $2,963 approx) per night from September 10 to 13, with the rates going back to normal from September 14th, a search on a travel app showed.

BRICS is an 11-member bloc which brings together major emerging markets and developing countries of the world.&#160;

India said the upcoming&#160;meet will also be joined by partner countries and outreach invitees.&#160;

India, which is also a founding member of BRICS, has previously held the presidency thrice —&#160; in 2012, 2016 and 2021.&#160;

India's BRICS chairship is guided by the theme of&#160;"Building for Resilience, Innovation, Cooperation and Sustainability,"&#160;according to a statement by the foreign ministry in New Delhi.&#160;

